`,o.jsx(t.p,{children:"Nepal is known for its mountains, but not nearly enough for the incredible high-altitude teas grown on its slopes. If you're looking for a souvenir that's uniquely Nepali and a little less cliché, tea deserves a place on your list."}),`
`,o.jsxs(t.p,{children:["My favourite place to buy tea is ",o.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Nepal Tea Collective"}),". They source organic tea from the hills of eastern Nepal, and I've found their teas to be consistently excellent. My personal favourites are Heart (Herbal Hibiscus Blend) and Boost (Spearmint Tea Blend), as I usually prefer caffeine-free teas."]}),`
`,o.jsxs(t.p,{children:["That said, I'd encourage you to try a few for yourself. They also run tea tasting experiences at places like ",o.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://ktmgh.com/kathmandu-guest-house/homepage/",children:"Kathmandu Guest House"})," in Thamel. So, if you're unsure what to buy, it's a fun way to sample different varieties of Nepali tea before deciding."]}),`
